<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Tarraco</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Tarraco was a Roman city on the coast of north-eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spain">Spain</a>, the predecessor of modern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tarragona">Tarragona</a>. Founded as a military base by the Scipio brothers in 218 BCE during the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/second-punic-war">Second Punic War</a>, it became the capital of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hispania-citerior">Hispania Citerior</a> and later of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hispania">Hispania</a> Tarraconensis, the largest Roman province in Spain. Its amphitheatre, walls and other remains are a World Heritage Site.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/tarraco.jpg" alt="Tarraco" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Rafa Esteve · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Tarragona_-_Amfiteatre_04_2016-08-31.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
